# Project Architecture

Read `docs/ai-context.md` and nearby source before broad changes.

- The single app is a Vite + React + TypeScript Pixi (WebGL2) texture-shader playground at `src/playground/**`. Entry point is `src/playground/main.tsx` → `TexturePlayground.tsx`. It renders an image/video into a duotone stripe-grid texture with baked letters and effects.
- Shared leaves: `src/components/{Button,HexColorPopover,pixi}`, `src/lib/cn.ts`, `src/theme/colorSpace.ts`, `src/grid/{prng,clipboard}.ts`, `src/fonts/codeSnippet.ts`.
- The React-export pipeline lives in `src/lib/export/**`.
- The pure grid math (`src/grid/config.ts`, `mask.ts`, `prng.ts`, `generator.ts`, `validate.ts`, `types.ts`) must stay free of React, DOM, Canvas, and browser APIs.
- `src/grid/clipboard.ts` is a legacy integration helper around grid serialization; keep it out of the pure grid math modules.
- `src/components/` owns reusable React UI and shared controls.
- Do not edit `.cursor/plans` unless the user explicitly asks.
- A pnpm-workspace restructure (packages/stripes-shader + apps/studio) and an installable render package are planned — see docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-17-stripes-shader-refactor-design.md.
